id: pm-58yzil
title: Enable explicit successful-command Sentry tracing without eager startup
description: "A fresh24h Sentry trace query returned zero rows after a successful read with SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=1. Successful-command span helpers require an already-initialized client, while current CLI initialization is lazy on error-reporting paths. Preserve that completed startup optimization and add an explicit, bounded tracing opt-in that can initialize and flush successful command spans without manufacturing errors."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: feature,observability,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-12T19:21:47.566Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T09:23:18.315Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-13T08:39:42.089Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-13T08:39:42.089Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Prove an independent successful-command opt-in control before and after; honor consent opt-outs and Vitest isolation; sanitize span context; preserve default cold-start and import budgets; verify one recent explicitly sampled trace through the authenticated Sentry API, distinguishing ingestion unavailability from source behavior."
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Export ensureSentryCommandTracing, initialize only for explicit positive sampling and effective consent, annotate streamed command spans, and flush completion within the existing bounded timeout."
expected_result: Opted-in successful commands produce useful recent sanitized spans while default startup and opt-out isolation remain lazy.
actual_result: "80 linked Sentry tests pass with real loopback export and configured opt-outs; independent initialization removal fails; authenticated Sentry discovery shows a real recent pm context span, and final Node/Bun/npx/bunx package workflows pass."
